<div class="blurb">
<div class="header"><h1>bbsengine</h1></div>
<div class="body">

<ul>
<li><b>what is it?</b> - bbsengine is an open source (GPLv2+) application platform that primarily uses
text interfaces with a web version available</li>
<li><b>what can it do?</b> - bbsengine has been used to build office applications ("projectflow") as well as games ("empyre" for starters).
 <ul>
  <li>ANSI escape sequences are a standard for in-band signaling to control cursor location, color, font styling, and other options on video text terminals</li>
  <li>support for vt102 and ECMA-48 (also known as ISO/IEC 6429 or ANSI X3.64) for
color, </li>
  <li><a href="https://vt100.net/">vt100.net</a></li>
 <li> io
  <ul>
  <li> echo()</li>
  <li> getch()</li>
  <li> inputchoice(), inputstring(), etc</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li> session management</li>
 <li> user authentication and management</li>
 <li> database management including roles</li>
 <li> some of the utilities:
  <ul>
  <li> pluralize()</li>
  <li> oxfordcomma()</li>
  <li> diceroll()</li>
  <li> hr() - horizontal rule, like in HTML</li>
  <li> heading() - a box with centered text inside it</li>
  </ul>
 </li>
 </ul>
</li>
<li><b>how do I get it?</b> - 20250515: there are no public downloads of bbsengine available at this time</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>the first release of bbsengine is dated 200401181647 (ET)</li>
<li><b>bbsengine.org</b> was registered on 2008-10-11</li>
{*<li>In June 2011 use of <a href="//pear.php.net/html_page2">html_page2</a> (requires 0.6.5-beta or above) was added and an upgrade to <a href="//smarty.net/">Smarty3</a> from smarty2 was
performed.</li>*}

{*<p>To make effective use of bbsengine4 you will need to be a developer
comfortable with the use of PEAR packages, Smarty3 Templates, and have
hosting with PostgreSQL available.  bbsengine4 has not been tested on
servers using web-based control panels for system administration.  it can be
done.  </p>*}
</ul>
</div>
</div>

